# Every file here is text, and docs/app.js is a build output that gets
# committed. With Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) a fresh clone
# checks the source out as CRLF, so `npm run build` on that machine emits a
# bundle that differs from the committed one on line endings alone — a 300KB
# phantom diff on a file that is actually deployed. Pinning LF everywhere means
# any machine builds the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf
